## 4. File Pattern Configuration

### 4.1 Pattern Types

#### Exact Match
```
'file_pattern': 'TM199C5.xlsm'
```
- Matches: TM199C5.xlsm only
- Use when: Processing specific named file

#### Wildcard Pattern
```
'file_pattern': 'MI_Forecast*.xlsm'
```
- Matches: MI_Forecast_Jan.xlsm, MI_Forecast_Feb.xlsm, etc.
- Use when: Processing multiple related files

#### Complex Pattern
```
'file_pattern': 'Report_Q[1-4]_*.xlsm'
```
- Matches: Report_Q1_2024.xlsm, Report_Q2_Final.xlsm, etc.
- Use when: Specific naming structure required

### 4.2 Pattern Examples

| Pattern | Matches | Use Case |
|---------|---------|----------|
| `'*.xlsm'` | All .xlsm files | Process all files |
| `'Monthly_*.xlsm'` | Monthly_Jan.xlsm, Monthly_Feb.xlsm | Monthly reports |
| `'*_Summary.xlsm'` | Q1_Summary.xlsm, Annual_Summary.xlsm | Summary files |
| `'Recon_202411*.xlsm'` | Recon_20241101.xlsm, Recon_20241130.xlsm | November 2024 files |

